cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to this material, please cite it as below. It describes a research program whose primary lane was paused on 2026-10-15; cite the snapshot date."
title: "CIR: cost-to-capability research on AI architectures and learning systems (research repository)"
type: generic
authors:
  - name: "DotrixAI"
    website: "https://dotrixai.com"
version: "2026-10-16"
date-released: "2026-10-16"
url: "https://dotrixai.com/cir"
repository: "https://github.com/DotrixAI/cir-research"
abstract: >-
  CIR is a DotrixAI research program on the training compute needed to reach a
  given capability, compared with strong optimized Transformer systems. Its primary
  lane was paused on 2026-10-15 after the target was not reached. This repository
  documents the objective, methodology, evidence, negative and superseded results,
  limitations and the reasons for the pause. It does not contain the CIR
  implementation.
keywords:
  - cost-to-capability
  - efficient language models
  - recurrent models
  - delta rule
  - baselines
  - training compute
  - pre-registration
  - research methodology
